# Lessons Learned

Following the power outage:

* Data remained intact.
* ZFS snapshots proved extremely valuable.
* Nextcloud required repair.
* SMB ACLs required repair.
* Home Assistant recovered successfully.

Future maintenance should always follow this process:

1. Create snapshot.
2. Run replication.
3. Verify backup completion.
4. Perform maintenance.

This ensures a recoverable restore point always exists before making system changes.

---

# Final Architecture

```text
                    Users
                      │
          SMB + Nextcloud Access
                      │
                8TB mainpool
                      │
          Monthly Recursive Snapshot
                      │
                      ▼
             Monthly Replication
                      │
                      ▼
              2TB backup-pool
             (Hidden from users)
                      │
             Disaster Recovery Only
```
